gold_comments_all.body:
[suggestion] Sorry that this suggestion is out of the scope of this PR.

I think that `context.lexer` should be put in a more proper place, e.g., `result.stylelint.lexer`, because `context.lexer` is an internal property and should always be present.

Currently, it's in the `context` argument called by the public API [`checkAgainstRule()`](https://stylelint.io/developer-guide/plugins/#stylelintutilscheckagainstrule):
https://github.com/stylelint/stylelint/blob/d750a6aeafb09973289f6a930a720d497720e8f0/lib/utils/checkAgainstRule.mjs#L16

Then, we have to consider a case where the `context` might be absent, since users might pass an arbitrary `context`.

If we had `result.stylelint.lexer`, we could make some code unnecessary, e.g.,

```ts
import type { Lexer as CSSTreeLexer } from 'css-tree';

// ...

/** @internal */
export type StylelintPostcssResult = {
  // ...
  lexer: CSSTreeLexer;
};
```

If anyone is concerned, I'll create a PR to implement the refactoring suggestion.

